CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* direct call: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* virtual call: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^\[.*pointer_dereference.*: FAILURE$
--
g++ 13 (-fsanitize=address,undefined) and clang++ 18 accept this program,
and it fails only its WRONG assertion.  Fixed: the thunk for B's vtable
slot kept D::self's return type D *, which did not fit the slot, and D's
virtual table object was not created at all (both assertions failed with
dereference failures).
